    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1596-26": {
      "title": "1596-26 Administration & Research Officer (Internal only)",
      "description": "1596-26 Administration & Research Officer (Internal only) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Administration & Research Officer (Internal only) School of Law & Social Sciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £31,236 to £36,636 Grade: Grade 07 Contract Type: Fixed Term\n              \n                (24 months) Basis: Part Time\n            (0.51) Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 28 October 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 18 November 2026 Reference: 1596-26 Release Date: Wednesday 14 October 2026 An exciting opportunity has arisen to join an interdisciplinary project team working on a Research England-funded project called ‘Artificial Intelligence Researcher Development Network Plus’ (AI.RDN+). This four-year project is evaluating the take-up of publicly available AI tools for doctoral research, promoting their responsible use and creating training, support and guidance for stakeholders across the doctoral ecosystem. You will provide proactive support for all aspects of the project, including servicing project consultations and meetings. You will co-ordinate the production of the AI.RDN+ Newsletter and other regular communications using digital media and will contribute to maintaining up-to-date information about the project on the AI.RDN+ website. You will liaise frequently with all project stakeholders and manage external enquiries. You will support data collection and analysis and contribute to the preparation of key project outputs. You will have proven experience of providing administrative support for complex interdisciplinary projects and experience of undertaking, writing up and presenting the results of qualitative research. You will have proven experience of data collection, especially as this relates to postgraduate researchers’ use of generative AI tools. You will possess excellent interpersonal and organisational skills and demonstrable experience of working effectively with internal and external stakeholders in the doctoral research ecosystem. Please visit our website http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate Compliance Officer Administration & Research Officer (Internal only) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1155-26": {
      "title": "Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate",
      "description": "1155-26 Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate Aston Business School Location: Birmingham City Centre Salary: £35,000 to £37,000\r\n            per annum with an additional budget for the duration of the project for professional and personal development Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (18 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Friday 06 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 04 December 2026 Reference: 1155-26 Release Date: Friday 16 October 2026 This position offers a unique opportunity for a highly motivated individual to work at the interface of academia and industry in a Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP) Associate role that will deliver transformational impact. You will lead and deliver a service innovation programme within a fast-growing British SME manufacturer, helping to drive innovation and business growth in a company with strong values centred on teamwork, innovation, and excellence. The project is fundamentally focused on servitization; supporting an engineering company transition from providing equipment through traditional capital expenditure (CapEx) systems towards a service-led, lifecycle-oriented business model. You will lead the co-design and implementation of a product-service system within the company, developing service-led concepts and offerings that create value for customers over the lifecycle of their operations. This role is designed to enable the transition of a company towards a service-led business model, developing new forms of value creation and strengthening long-term customer relationships. You will play a key role in establishing the foundations for ongoing servitization, embedding new capabilities, and supporting the sustainable growth of the business beyond the duration of the KTP. Candidate Profile : A minimum of a 2:1 BSc degree in Engineering or Management, or a related discipline. Essential skills, experience and attributes required include: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Ability to work across technical and commercial domains Experience of adapting theories and/or tools to commercial practice Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills with the ability to engage across multiple levels of an organisation Strong project management capability, able to manage complex projects, coordinate roles, and work independently, as well as part of the team. Commercially aware and able to link innovation to business value Organised, adaptable and able to work effectively in an interdisciplinary collaborative environment Desirable for the role: A postgraduate qualification (or equivalent experience) in a relevant field, such as Engineering Management, Service Design, Operations, Innovation, or Marketing. Knowledge or experience of servitization, product-service systems, or business model innovation. Experience of working in manufacturing or industrial settings. Experience in customer research, data analysis, or development of commercially informed strategies. Key responsibilities of this role include: Service design and product-service system development Servitization strategy development Commercial and go-to-market activities Customer and stakeholder engagement Knowledge transfer and embedding Academic contribution to conference papers/ journal publications See the job description for full details of the responsibilities associated with this role. Additional Benefits and support: Up to £4,000 for personal and professional development for the duration of the project Annual leave (25 days p/a) Professional support and mentorship Mental Health and wellbeing support: https://www.aston.ac.uk/staff-public/hr/Benefits-and-Rewards/health-wellbeing A flexible blend of on-site and remote working arrangements can be negotiated in case of positive ongoing performance. Career prospects: This role opens up exciting career opportunities in new business development and servitization. Over 60% of our KTP associates are offered employment by their host companies at the end of the KTP. This is a Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP). It is essential you understand how KTP works and the vital role you will play if you secure this position. To learn more please visit: www.aston.ac.uk/ktp The Company: A Birmingham-based, industry-leading manufacturer, specialised in engineering and producing material handling equipment. Aston University: You will work in a project team consisting of Dr Reza Marvi, Dr Geoff Parkes, Dr Daniel Andrews from Aston University and the Senior Management Team of the Company, with the support of a Knowledge Transfer Adviser from Innovate UK. Location: The successful candidate will be based in central Birmingham , West Midlands, with regular access to Aston University facilities. Occasional travel to client sites across the UK will be required. The successful candidate must reside within a reasonable commuting distance of the work base. For informal enquiries about this role please contact Dr Reza Marvi, e-mail: r.marvi@aston.ac.uk If you think this isn’t the right opportunity for you, please explore other KTP vacancies across the country: https://www.ktp-uk.org/jobs/ This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent&nbsp ; It is an Innovate UK requirement that candidates hold a visa or immigration permission to cover the full duration of the contract. The successful candidate is therefore expected to apply for a visa as necessary in line with their contract duration. Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate Compliance Officer Administration & Research Officer (Internal only) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1447-26": {
      "title": "1447-26 Business Hub Receptionist",
      "description": "1447-26 Business Hub Receptionist - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Business Hub Receptionist Campus Services Location: 10 Woodcock St Salary: £26,707 to £27,865\n            per annum Grade: Grade 05 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 09 November 2026 Interview Date: Monday 23 November 2026 Reference: 1447-26 Release Date: Tuesday 20 October 2026 An exciting opportunity has arisen to join Aston University as a Business Hub Receptionist, providing a welcoming and professional service at a space designed to support innovative start-ups and growing businesses. Based at Aston Business Hub on Woodcock Street, you will be the first point of contact for tenants, visitors, staff and students. The Hub will accommodate up to 100 entrepreneurial businesses working in areas including artificial intelligence, digital systems and data science, connecting them with the University’s expertise and facilities. You will deliver excellent customer service, manage telephone and email enquiries, arrange visitor bookings and issue passes. You will help tenants connect with relevant University colleagues, undertake initial security ID checks, report faults and maintain a welcoming reception area. Working within a small team, you will provide flexible cover and support other University sites when required. You will have a good general education to GCSE level or equivalent, proven reception or administrative experience, and excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Confidence using Microsoft Office, a professional telephone manner and the ability to work independently and collaboratively are essential. You will handle challenging situations calmly and maintain high standards of confidentiality and security. A customer service qualification, experience supporting small businesses or working in education, and familiarity with a PC-based switchboard would be advantageous. For informal enquiries, contact William Morgan, Head of Security, at w.morgan3@aston.ac.uk . What we offer: Aston University is a vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 25 days bookable leave Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family-friendly policies. On-site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available. Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1629-26": {
      "title": "1629-26 Programme & Student Admin Officer",
      "description": "1629-26 Programme & Student Admin Officer - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Programme & Student Admin Officer Chief Student Officer Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £31,236 to £36,636\n            per annum Grade: Grade 07 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Sunday 01 November 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 17 November 2026 Reference: 1629-26 Release Date: Monday 19 October 2026 We are seeking an experienced and highly organised Programme and Student Administration Officer to join our Academic Registry team. This role is central to the delivery of key student administration processes, supporting students throughout their academic journey and ensuring the effective operation of programme and assessment related activities. Please note, there are x3 positions available. What you will do Oversee the day-to-day delivery of programme operations and assessment and awards activities across designated areas. Provide supervision, guidance and workload coordination for Programme and Student Administration Coordinators. Act as the first point of escalation for operational issues, complex student cases and process queries. Coordinate key academic processes including programme and module administration, Boards of Examiners, progression and award activities. Ensure high standards of data quality, regulatory compliance and customer service. Support continuous improvement through process enhancement, training and systems development. Build effective relationships with academic colleagues and professional services teams to assist successful service delivery. What we are looking for Experience of supervising, coordinating or guiding colleagues within a similar administrative environment. Experience of working within Higher Education or another complex and regulated environment. Experience of managing complex or sensitive cases and applying policies, procedures and regulations. Excellent organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Strong analytical, communication and problem-solving skills. A commitment to delivering high-quality, student-focused services. Further information A degree or evidence of continuing professional development, and knowledge of Tribal SITS would be advantageous. Regular on-campus engagement is required in line with academic and service needs. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor the successful candidate if they are eligible for one of the salary discount options. Please see here for details about when you can be paid less for a Skilled Worker visa: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa/when-you-can-be-paid-less&nbsp ;Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1775-26": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Biochemistry",
      "description": "1775-26 Lecturer in Biochemistry - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Lecturer in Biochemistry Medicine, Pharmacy & Biosciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £39,560 to £57,666\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 to Grade 09 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Friday 04 December 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 05 January 2027 Reference: 1775-26 Release Date: Wednesday 21 October 2026 The Department of Biosciences is driven by an ambitious research and teaching strategy within the School of Medicine, Pharmacy & Biosciences, the Aston Centre for Health in Ageing and the Aston Institute for Membrane Excellence.  We are seeking to build upon and develop our established research strengths and wish to appoint a new colleague to contribute to the research, impact and teaching profile within Biosciences at Aston University. As a successful School we offer a friendly, supportive and vibrant community to enable world-leading research. Applicants must have a PhD in a Biosciences-related area that will complement our School’s excellent research.  They will be able to evidence an independent and strongly developing research programme, preferably including securing external research funding and publications in high-ranking, peer-reviewed journals.  Applicants must have the ability to develop internationally recognised activity. The Department has a strong focus on the application of fundamental research. We are particularly interested in receiving applications from individuals who can demonstrate research excellence focused on the use of molecular and biochemical approaches to understand health and disease or biotechnological processes.  Applicants with a research profile focused on biochemistry, biophysics and/or engineering biology are particularly encouraged to apply. All applicants must demonstrate an alignment with our existing research programmes and ideally be able to strengthen our research through their addition to our team. Applicants should also be able to demonstrate a developing track record of effective teaching and an enthusiasm for delivering flexible education across the range of programmes within the School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences.  Previous experience of teaching Biochemistry and/or Biotechnology would be advantageous. Any application must be able to demonstrate your necessary teamwork skills to foster collaboration with existing Biosciences colleagues and to build links both within the University and externally, including the aptitude and ability to engage in continuous professional development. You should clearly state how your appointment will build further critical mass within the School and support the University mission through high quality, exploitable research that is accessible for business and has a positive impact on society. Potential applicants may wish to contact the Head of Biosciences, Professor Alan Goddard ( a.goddard@aston.ac.uk ), the Director of Research, Dr Alice Rothnie ( a.rothnie@aston.ac.uk ) and/or the Director for Education Dr Charlotte Law ( c.law@aston.ac.uk ) for informal discussion about the post before applying. Our web site at http://www1.aston.ac.uk/ provides further details of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences, Aston Research Centre for Health in Ageing and the new Aston Institute for Membrane Excellence( https://www.aston.ac.uk/research/aime ). Aston University is committed to the principles of the Athena SWAN Charter, recognised by a Gold award. We pride ourselves on our vibrant, friendly, supportive working environment and collaborative atmosphere. Please visit our website http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Description University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1724-26": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Civil Engineering",
      "description": "1724-26 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Civil Engineering - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Civil Engineering School of Engineering & Innovation Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £48,337 to £68,817\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 09 to Grade 10 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Saturday 14 November 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 08 December 2026 Reference: 1724-26 Release Date: Tuesday 20 October 2026 Civil and Logistics Engineering is a growing and ambitious department, bringing together expertise across Civil Engineering, Transport, Supply Chain and Engineering Management. We are looking for an enthusiastic and collaborative academic in Geotechnical Engineering to contribute to our teaching, research and wider departmental activity. We particularly welcome applicants who can connect geotechnical engineering with challenges facing the West Midlands , including infrastructure renewal, brownfield regeneration, resilient transport, sustainable construction, climate adaptation and the transition to net zero. We value teamwork, collegiality and an inclusive environment , with a shared commitment to delivering an outstanding student experience. The successful applicant will contribute through: • Developing research projects, proposals and publications in geotechnical engineering and related areas, including infrastructure resilience, sustainable geotechnics, geohazards and geoenvironmental engineering. • Building research impact and knowledge exchange in collaboration with external stakeholders. • Supporting students through project supervision, laboratory and field-based learning, and industrial placements. • Creating meaningful student opportunities through employer engagement, site visits, guest lectures, mentoring and collaborative projects, particularly across the West Midlands. We are looking for candidates with qualifications and experience in Geotechnical Engineering , with expertise in one or more of the following: • Site investigation, soil and rock mechanics, foundations and earthworks. • Ground improvement, geosynthetics, slopes, retaining structures and infrastructure. • Climate-resilient infrastructure, transport, brownfield regeneration or urban ground engineering. • Geohazards, ground–structure interaction, earthquake engineering or numerical and physical modelling. • Geoenvironmental engineering, sustainable materials, circular construction or low-carbon geotechnical solutions. Expertise in sustainability, resilience or digital geotechnics would be particularly welcomed. You will also be committed to supporting a diverse range of learners and contributing positively to an inclusive, supportive and collegiate community . Impact in the West Midlands A key part of the role will be helping to establish Aston University as a regional hub for geotechnical knowledge, skills and innovation. You will work collaboratively with stakeholders to create authentic learning experiences and strengthen pathways into civil and geotechnical engineering for students across the region. What we offer: • Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. • Excellent training and development opportunities. • A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. • Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers • Great family friendly policies • On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available • Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Please visit our website https://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. Further details: Job Description University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
