    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1255-26": {
      "title": "Apprentice Technician",
      "description": "1255-26 Apprentice Technician - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Apprentice Technician School Operations (COO) Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £21,366 to £25,166 Grade: Apprentice Grade 05 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (31/08/2031) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 18 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 09 December 2026 Reference: 1255-26 Release Date: Wednesday 21 October 2026 Aston University is a leading university in the heart of Birmingham, known for its focus on employability, real‑world impact and an inclusive, supportive culture. The opportunity An exciting opportunity has arisen to join our amazing technical team within School Operations to join our Vision Sciences Technical Team as an Apprentice Technician. We are seeking a proactive, reliable individual to join our team which supports teaching and research facilities. The successful candidate will provide practical and technical support across the School of Optometry, including the Aston Eye Clinic, clinical skills spaces, teaching laboratories and dispensing-related learning areas. The post will help ensure that teaching rooms, clinics, equipment and consumables are prepared to a high standard, supporting a positive experience for students, staff, supervisors and patients. This is a varied and rewarding role where you will work closely with technical colleagues, academic staff, and students to ensure our clinics run smoothly, safely, and effectively. The main responsibilities of this role include: Assist with the setup and preparation of optometry and audiology teaching clinics, practical sessions and clinical skills spaces. Check rooms, equipment, computers, test charts and teaching resources before sessions begin, escalating any issues appropriately. Support the issuing, tracking, cleaning and safe return of clinical and teaching equipment. Help maintain stock levels of consumables, frames, lenses and other teaching or clinic supplies. Maintain tidy, safe and professional working areas in line with local procedures and health and safety requirements. Support staff, supervisors and students during teaching sessions where required. Develop knowledge of dispensing, optical appliances, frame handling, lens types and clinic workflow as preparation for the apprenticeship pathway. Complete agreed training records, reflective notes and development objectives as part of the in-house training programme. About you We are looking for a practical, organised, proactive individual with a strong commitment to teamwork and customer service. You will thrive in a busy, dynamic environment and enjoy working collaboratively with a diverse range of people, from students to academic staff and external suppliers. Excellent communication skills and a strong attention to detail are essential for supporting practical classes and demonstrating equipment. Training and Development Pathway In-house technical training: The apprentice will receive supervised training across clinic preparation, equipment checks, stock control, health and safety, basic maintenance tasks, patient-facing professionalism and support for teaching sessions. Dispensing Optician apprenticeship: Completing a recognised Dispensing Optician apprenticeship pathway, combining workplace learning with formal study. Ongoing support: The apprentice will receive regular supervision, feedback, probation/development conversations and opportunities to build confidence through practical experience. Working at Aston We are committed to the Technician Commitment and to supporting the career development of technical staff across all disciplines. You will be supported to undertake a range of training and development activity, as a minimum, you will undertake relevant technical and health & safety training. Aston University is located within Birmingham city centre and benefits from excellent transport links by bus and train. Discounted on-site parking and a cycle-to-work scheme are also available. Information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . For further Information, please contact the Technical Team Leader – Matthew Hancock m.hancock@aston.ac.uk Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) Apprentice Technician Lecturer in Biochemistry View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1825-26": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only)",
      "description": "1825-26 Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) Aston Institute of Materials Engineering Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £40,704\r\n            per annum (pro-rata) Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (12 months) Basis: Part Time\r\n            (18.25 hours per week) Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Sunday 08 November 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Reference: 1825-26 Release Date: Tuesday 27 October 2026 Applicants are invited to apply for a Postdoctoral Research Associate (PDRA) part-time position 0.5 FTE on the funded project “Biomanufacturing microbots for next generation bacterial theranostics to tackle metastatic solid tumours”, supported by the Yorkshire MedTech Place Based Impact Accelerator Account (PBIAA). The project aims to establish the feasibility of producing robust, living magnetic microcarriers for future applications in cancer imaging and targeted therapeutic delivery. The role will focus on developing and evaluating biomanufacturing processes for magnetotactic bacteria, which naturally produce magnetic nanoparticles called magnetosomes. Working with Magnetospirillum gryphiswaldense MSR-1, the successful candidate will contribute to the cultivation and characterisation of thermotolerant strains assessing growth, viability, motility and magnetic properties at elevated temperatures. The post holder will also develop and evaluate a continuous biomanufacturing workflow, integrating controlled bioreactor cultivation with cell harvesting and downstream processing. This will include comparing cross-flow filtration with conventional centrifugation to improve cell recovery and purity while preserving viability, motility and magnetic properties. The work will generate reproducible experimental datasets and protocols to support scale-up and future translation. The successful applicant will hold a PhD qualification, or be close to completion of a relevant PhD, in biotechnology, biochemical engineering, microbiology, industrial biotechnology, chemical engineering or a related discipline. Essential hands-on skills include experience in microbial cultivation, fermentation or bioprocess development, experimental design, sample preparation and quantitative data analysis. The ability to plan and carry out laboratory experiments independently, troubleshoot experimental problems and maintain accurate research records is essential. Expertise in one or more of the following areas will be particularly advantageous: cultivation of magnetotactic bacteria or other microaerophilic microorganisms; controlled bioreactor operation; adaptive laboratory evolution or microbial strain characterisation; cross-flow or tangential-flow filtration; continuous bioprocessing; flow cytometry; microscopy and motility assays; and characterisation of cellular magnetic properties. An interest in biomanufacturing for biomedical applications and an awareness of quality requirements relevant to future manufacturing development would also be valuable. Strong organisational, communication and teamwork skills are important, as the post holder will work within a multidisciplinary collaboration involving academic and industrial partners. Knowledge of laboratory safety, good research practice and data management is essential. The successful candidate will contribute to project meetings, technical reports and deliverables, and communicate findings to collaborators. The ability to develop new technical expertise and meet project milestones within a short, focused research programme is highly desirable. For informal enquiries about this position, please contact Dr Alfred Fernandez-Castane at a.fernandez-castane1@aston.ac.uk . Please note this vacancy is open to internal applicants only. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Description University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Research Associate Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1829-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "1829-26 Research Associate - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Associate Psychology, Health & Clinical Sci School Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £41,885 to £46,970\r\n            per annum (pro-rata) Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (30/08/2030) Basis: Part Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 30 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 16 December 2026 Reference: 1829-26 Release Date: Wednesday 28 October 2026 An excellent opportunity has arisen for an experienced and motivated researcher to join our multidisciplinary team of researchers, clinical psychologists and psychiatrists working on LADDERS, a £2.29 million national randomised controlled trial funded by the NIHR Health Technology Assessment (HTA) Programme. The trial is evaluating a parent-mediated anxiety intervention for children with moderate to severe intellectual disabilities and aims to improve access to evidence-based psychological support for children and families. The successful applicant will be affiliated with the Aston Institute for Health & Neurodevelopment and work collaboratively with researchers at University College London (UCL), Leicester Clinical Trials Unit and NHS partners across the UK. Flexible hybrid and remote working arrangements are supported. The researcher will take independent responsibility for defined aspects of the trial, including coordinating participant recruitment, conducting assessments of eligibility against protocol-defined clinical criteria and undertaking blinded outcome assessments. They will contribute to the methodological and scientific delivery of the research, ensuring high standards of data quality and research governance, and play an active role in data analysis, academic publications and dissemination. The role will also involve supporting and supervising students and collaborating with researchers and clinical partners across the UK. We welcome applications from candidates with a PhD in psychology, health, behavioural science or a related discipline, or equivalent qualifications and substantial relevant research experience. Experience in mental health assessment or research involving children and young people with intellectual disabilities would be particularly valuable. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Description University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Research Associate Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) Lecturer in People Management (0.4% FTE Fixed Term) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1749-26": {
      "title": "Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate)",
      "description": "1749-26 Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate) Medicine, Pharmacy & Biosciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £48,337 to £57,666 Grade: Grade 09 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Thursday 12 November 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 03 December 2026 Reference: 1749-26 Release Date: Thursday 29 October 2026 Are you an experienced clinician and educator who is passionate about developing the next generation of healthcare professionals? We are seeking an enthusiastic and experienced Clinical Teaching Fellow to join our Physician Associate Programme. This is a teaching-intensive role offering the opportunity to make a visible and lasting contribution to students’ clinical knowledge, professional development and readiness for practice. You will teach across the programme using a range of interactive and student-centred approaches. These include whole-cohort teaching, problem-based learning, team-based learning and small-group clinical skills teaching. You will help students integrate biomedical and clinical knowledge and develop their clinical reasoning, consultation, communication, examination and practical procedural skills. We are looking for an experienced clinician who is confident teaching across the breadth of the curriculum and able to translate contemporary clinical practice into engaging, evidence-informed learning. You will contribute to teaching, assessment, student support, curriculum development and programme enhancement, with opportunities to become involved in simulation, educational innovation, scholarship and development projects. You will be a proactive self-starter who can take ownership of areas of work, manage competing priorities and work independently. Equally, you will enjoy contributing to a close and collaborative programme team within Aston Medical School and working with colleagues across the wider School of Medicine, Pharmacy and Biosciences. Applicants should have substantial post-qualification clinical experience, current professional registration and established experience of teaching healthcare learners. Experience of designing and delivering practical clinical skills teaching is particularly important. A postgraduate qualification in medical or healthcare education is highly desirable, alongside professional recognition such as Fellowship of Advance HE or the Academy of Medical Educators. If you are an experienced clinician-educator who genuinely enjoys teaching and wants to see the direct impact of your work on students, we would be delighted to hear from you. Applicants looking for part time hours will be considered What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role may meet the requirements for Skilled Worker visa sponsorship. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate) Research Associate Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=R260050": {
      "title": "Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate",
      "description": "R260050 Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Servitization and Service Innovation Lead – KTP Associate Aston Business School Location: Birmingham City Centre Salary: £35,000 to £37,000\r\n            per annum with an additional budget for the duration of the project for professional and personal development Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (18 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Friday 06 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 04 December 2026 Reference: R260050 Release Date: Tuesday 06 October 2026 This position offers a unique opportunity for a highly motivated individual to work at the interface of academia and industry in a Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP) Associate role that will deliver transformational impact. You will lead and deliver a service innovation programme within a fast-growing British SME manufacturer, helping to drive innovation and business growth in a company with strong values centred on teamwork, innovation, and excellence. The project is fundamentally focused on servitization; supporting an engineering company transition from providing equipment through traditional capital expenditure (CapEx) systems towards a service-led, lifecycle-oriented business model. You will lead the co-design and implementation of a product-service system within the company, developing service-led concepts and offerings that create value for customers over the lifecycle of their operations. This role is designed to enable the transition of a company towards a service-led business model, developing new forms of value creation and strengthening long-term customer relationships. You will play a key role in establishing the foundations for ongoing servitization, embedding new capabilities, and supporting the sustainable growth of the business beyond the duration of the KTP. Candidate Profile : A minimum of a 2:1 BSc degree in Engineering or Management, or a related discipline. Essential skills, experience and attributes required include: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills Ability to work across technical and commercial domains Experience of adapting theories and/or tools to commercial practice Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills with the ability to engage across multiple levels of an organisation Strong project management capability, able to manage complex projects, coordinate roles, and work independently, as well as part of the team. Commercially aware and able to link innovation to business value Organised, adaptable and able to work effectively in an interdisciplinary collaborative environment Desirable for the role: A postgraduate qualification (or equivalent experience) in a relevant field, such as Engineering Management, Service Design, Operations, Innovation, or Marketing. Knowledge or experience of servitization, product-service systems, or business model innovation. Experience of working in manufacturing or industrial settings. Experience in customer research, data analysis, or development of commercially informed strategies. Key responsibilities of this role include: Service design and product-service system development Servitization strategy development Commercial and go-to-market activities Customer and stakeholder engagement Knowledge transfer and embedding Academic contribution to conference papers/ journal publications See the job description for full details of the responsibilities associated with this role. Additional Benefits and support: Up to £4,000 for personal and professional development for the duration of the project Annual leave (25 days p/a) Professional support and mentorship Mental Health and wellbeing support: https://www.aston.ac.uk/staff-public/hr/Benefits-and-Rewards/health-wellbeing A flexible blend of on-site and remote working arrangements can be negotiated in case of positive ongoing performance. Career prospects: This role opens up exciting career opportunities in new business development and servitization. Over 60% of our KTP associates are offered employment by their host companies at the end of the KTP. This is a Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP). It is essential you understand how KTP works and the vital role you will play if you secure this position. To learn more please visit: www.aston.ac.uk/ktp The Company: A Birmingham-based, industry-leading manufacturer, specialised in engineering and producing material handling equipment. Aston University: You will work in a project team consisting of Dr Reza Marvi, Dr Geoff Parkes, Dr Daniel Andrews from Aston University and the Senior Management Team of the Company, with the support of a Knowledge Transfer Adviser from Innovate UK. Location: The successful candidate will be based in central Birmingham , West Midlands, with regular access to Aston University facilities. Occasional travel to client sites across the UK will be required. The successful candidate must reside within a reasonable commuting distance of the work base. For informal enquiries about this role please contact Dr Reza Marvi, e-mail: r.marvi@aston.ac.uk If you think this isn’t the right opportunity for you, please explore other KTP vacancies across the country: https://www.ktp-uk.org/jobs/ This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent&nbsp ; It is an Innovate UK requirement that candidates hold a visa or immigration permission to cover the full duration of the contract. The successful candidate is therefore expected to apply for a visa as necessary in line with their contract duration. Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate) Research Associate Postdoctoral Research Associate (Internal Only) View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1778-26": {
      "title": "1778-26 Press and Communications Manager",
      "description": "1778-26 Press and Communications Manager - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Press and Communications Manager Marketing, Recruitment & Admissions Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £39,560 to £46,970 Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 16 November 2026 Interview Date: Monday 07 December 2026 Reference: 1778-26 Release Date: Friday 30 October 2026 Bring your news judgement, creativity and relationship-building skills to Aston University’s communications team, part of the Marketing, Communications and Student Recruitment department. The Press and Communications team protects and enhances Aston University’s reputation and delivers communications that support institutional priorities. Its audiences include prospective and current students, staff, alumni, partners, employers, policymakers and the wider public. We are looking for an experienced, enthusiastic and ambitious PR and communications professional to bring our research and expertise to wider audiences. You will work with journalists, write compelling press releases and other copy, support researchers to contribute expert commentary and analysis, and help produce podcasts and other multimedia content. This role will lead communications for Aston Business School and the School of Law and Social Sciences, alongside their associated research institutes. Reporting to the Head of Communications, you will also contribute to the University’s corporate communications and major institutional priorities. Collaboration will be central to your success. As a trusted professional adviser, you will bring people together around shared objectives, explain your recommendations clearly and offer constructive challenge where needed. This is an opportunity to combine strategic thinking with hands-on delivery. You will lead annual and project-based communications plans, identifying the strongest opportunities to showcase teaching, research, enterprise, engagement and impact. Alongside planned campaigns, you will respond to emerging opportunities and sensitive enquiries. Accuracy, accessibility and editorial integrity will underpin everything you produce. You will bring substantial professional experience in journalism and/or public relations. Experience of communicating complex subject matter, ideally within a business, law or social science environment, is ideal. Experience of coordinating contributors, managing agencies or suppliers, and commissioning or producing multimedia content will also help you deliver across this varied portfolio. Experience in research or higher education is desirable, but not essential. If you enjoy asking questions, finding the story behind complex ideas and working with others to achieve impact, this role offers scope to take ownership and contribute your professional expertise. Please visit our website http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Press and Communications Manager Clinical Teaching Fellow (Physician Associate) Research Associate View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1844-26": {
      "title": "1844-26 Student Centre Manager",
      "description": "1844-26 Student Centre Manager - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Student Centre Manager Chief Student Officer Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £39,560 to £46,970 Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 16 November 2026 Interview Date: Tuesday 01 December 2026 Reference: 1844-26 Release Date: Monday 02 November 2026 We are seeking a Student Solutions Centre (SSC) Manager to lead a welcoming, responsive and consistent first point of contact for students at Aston University. Part of Student Life, the SSC helps students resolve enquiries and access the right information, advice and specialist support throughout their studies. Reporting to the Head of Advice Services, you will manage the Student Centre Assistants and the Centre’s day-to-day operations across in-person, email, telephone and online channels. You will plan staffing and service cover, develop clear procedures, coordinate administrative support for Student Life teams and use service information and student feedback to improve the experience we provide. You will work closely with specialist colleagues, ensuring timely referrals and clear handovers while respecting their responsibilities and reporting lines. A key priority will be to lead attainment and ongoing maintenance of the Customer Service Excellence Award for the SSC, embedding evidence-led service standards and continuous improvement in day-to-day delivery. You will use ticketing and case management systems confidently, run reports on service standards and utilisation, and interpret operational data alongside student feedback to shape provision, allocate resources and evaluate improvements. Key Responsibilities and Priorities Lead welcoming, accessible and consistent front-line advice, enquiry handling and triage. Manage and develop Student Centre Assistants, setting clear expectations and supporting effective delivery. Plan workloads, rotas and available space to maintain service continuity during absence and peak demand. Agree practical referral, handover and administrative support arrangements with partner teams. Improve procedures, student-facing information and service delivery using feedback and enquiry trends. Lead attainment and maintenance of the Customer Service Excellence Award, coordinating evidence, improvement actions and ongoing review with the Head of Advice Services and relevant partners. Use ticketing and case management systems to maintain reliable service records, run reports on service standards, utilisation and demand, interpret trends and evidence, and translate findings into service provision and measurable improvements. Maintain accurate records and reporting, appropriate confidentiality and clear escalation arrangements. Provide operational health and safety support for the SSC, working with relevant University colleagues. About You You will bring significant staff management or supervisory experience in a fast-paced, customer-facing environment, alongside experience of coordinating service delivery and applying policies and procedures accurately. You will be an organised, collaborative communicator who can handle confidential information and challenging enquiries with tact, maintain clear professional boundaries and support colleagues under pressure. You will understand service processes from the student perspective and use feedback and operational information to make practical improvements. You will be educated to graduate level or have equivalent relevant experience, with strong written and administrative skills. You will be data literate and confident using ticketing and case management systems, running reports on service standards and utilisation, checking data quality and interpreting evidence to inform service provision and improvement. You will be able to translate findings into clear recommendations and evaluate the impact of changes. You will bring an evidence-led approach to attaining and maintaining the Customer Service Excellence Award. Experience in Higher or Further Education and a relevant professional qualification would be advantageous but are not essential. Experience of a particular product such as TopDesk is desirable; capability with relevant ticketing and case management systems is a core requirement. Please visit our website http://www.aston.ac.uk/jobs for further information and to apply online. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Senior Lecturer Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management Student Centre Manager View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1224-26": {
      "title": "1224-26 Student Wellbeing Case Manager",
      "description": "1224-26 Student Wellbeing Case Manager - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Student Wellbeing Case Manager Chief Student Officer Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £38,784 to £46,970\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 30 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 16 December 2026 Reference: 1224-26 Release Date: Sunday 01 November 2026 Aston University’s 2030 strategy is Inclusive, Entrepreneurial and Transformational. We are building a new model of university for a changing world, delivering measurable impact for our students, staff, partners and communities. Within this vision, the Student Life Directorate plays a central role in assisting students from transition through to successful completion, providing expert guidance on engagement, wellbeing and student success. We are seeking a Student Wellbeing Case Manager to join Aston University’s Student Life Directorate. The role holder will provide expert oversight of complex wellbeing case management, triage coordination, caseload scheduling, risk escalation and defensible practice. This role will suit someone with strong professional judgement, excellent case coordination skills and the ability to maintain safe, consistent and defensible practice in a complex wellbeing environment. Key Responsibilities and Priorities Complex wellbeing, safeguarding and risk-related case oversight Triage, allocation, review and escalation processes Caseload scheduling and capacity monitoring Clear case summaries, recommendations and defensible records Calm, professional judgement in urgent, complex and ambiguous situations About You You will hold a relevant professional qualification in mental health, counselling, social work, nursing, psychology, occupational therapy, safeguarding or a related discipline, and have equivalent substantial professional experience. You bring significant experience in complex case management, triage, referral or risk-related work. You can remain calm and systematic when situations are urgent, sensitive or ambiguous. You understand the importance of high-quality records, professional boundaries and timely escalation. You can support practitioners and managers through effective oversight of caseloads, capacity and review points. You will be confident working within confidentiality, safeguarding, information-sharing and data protection requirements, maintaining accurate and defensible records in a high-accountability wellbeing environment. Experience within Higher Education, young adult support, clinical supervision processes, service scheduling or electronic case management systems would be advantageous. What We Offer A dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, with excellent transport links by bus and train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 25 days’ bookable leave and a further 13 days’ bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts for a range of activities and retailers. Great family-friendly policies. On-site gym and pool, with discounted staff membership available. Please complete the full application form, as CVs and cover letters are not visible to the shortlisting panel until after shortlisting has been completed. This role may meet the requirements for Skilled Worker visa sponsorship. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Senior Lecturer Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management Student Centre Manager View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1716-26": {
      "title": "Clinical Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "1716-26 Clinical Senior Lecturer - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Clinical Senior Lecturer Medicine, Pharmacy & Biosciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Grade: YC72 NHS 2003 Consultant Contract Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Part Time\r\n            (0.17) Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 18 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 11 December 2026 Reference: 1716-26 Release Date: Wednesday 04 November 2026 We are seeking to appoint an experienced and respected medical educator to lead our professional support and concerns processes and provide strategic oversight of professionalism and fitness to practise matters across the MBChB programme. The postholder will work closely with academic and professional services colleagues to promote a culture of professionalism, early intervention and student support. Reporting Relationships Reports to: Dean of Medical Education Accountable to: MBChB Board of Studies Responsible for: School Support and Concerns Committee Role Purpose To provide strategic leadership for the School's Support and Concerns Framework and act as the senior academic responsible for the management of professionalism, conduct, behaviour, wellbeing and student fitness to practise concerns. The postholder will oversee the review and investigation of concerns raised about medical students, ensure appropriate support and remediation are implemented, chair relevant committees, advise senior leadership on complex cases, and maintain compliance with General Medical Council (GMC) requirements and University regulations. What we offer Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role does not meet the eligibility criteria for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. See here for information about Skilled Worker eligibility criteria: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Senior Lecturer Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management Student Centre Manager View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=R260051": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management",
      "description": "R260051 Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management Aston Business School Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £38,784 to £56,535\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 to Grade 09 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 25 November 2026 Interview Date: Thursday 10 December 2026 Reference: R260051 Release Date: Wednesday 04 November 2026 Aston Business School is a triple accredited University (EQUIS, AACSB and AMBA) and a leading UK University for academic research (REF2021 rated 79% of Aston’s research as ‘world leading’ or ‘internationally excellent’ and 74% of research impact as ‘very considerable or ‘outstanding’). Aston prides itself on excellent teaching and business engagement. We are one of the few UK institutions with the Small Business Charter’s Gold Award. In 2020 we were The Guardian’s University of the Year and the THE’s Entrepreneurial University of the Year. We were shortlisted for THE’s University of the Year in 2021-22 and are in the QS Top 400 World University Rankings in 2026. The Business Analytics and Information Systems Department conducts teaching, research and engagement activities in various aspects of analytics and IS/ICT. The department fosters a thriving teaching innovation and research culture in the Department, which has a strong reputation for being both rigorous and relevant. As part of our growth strategy, we are seeking inspirational, inclusive and highly motivated professionals to contribute to the development of the Department’s teaching, PhD/DBA supervision, research and enterprise activities. We welcome discussions with prospective candidates whose teaching portfolio includes digital forensics, cybersecurity management, cryptocurrencies, blockchains and fintech. You will have a good first degree and a PhD in a relevant academic discipline. It would be desirable to be able to demonstrate an emerging record of funding, publication of research outputs and creation of research-based impacts in industry and/or society. We are especially looking for people with a strong research profile in the areas of VFAs and cryptocurrencies, blockchain and fintech. The applicant is expected to join the Cyber Security Innovation (CSI) Centre . The Centre brings together stakeholders from industry, government and prominent cybersecurity research institutions. The scope of the international Cyber Security & Innovation Centre is to strategically manage operations and build effective relationships across academia, industry, and policymakers. Aston University is committed to the Athena SWAN Charter http://www.ecu.ac.uk/equality-charter-marks/athena-swan/ recognized by a bronze award. We pride ourselves on our vibrant, friendly, supportive working environment and collaborative atmosphere. What\r\nwe offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Details University Information Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Clinical Senior Lecturer Lecturer in Cybersecurity Management Student Centre Manager View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1858-26": {
      "title": "1858-26 Assoc Dean",
      "description": "1858-26 Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills Aston Professional Location: Aston University John Cadbury House Salary: £59,390 to £68,817\n            per annum Grade: Grade 10 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 23 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 09 December 2026 Reference: 1858-26 Release Date: Friday 06 November 2026 We are seeking an experienced and influential senior leader to join Aston Professional as Associate Dean of Apprenticeships and Skills. This is an opportunity to shape high-quality, employer-responsive apprenticeship provision across the University, bringing together academic excellence, outstanding apprentice experiences and robust institutional assurance. Working collaboratively with the Director of Aston Professional, Schools and Professional Services, you will provide strategic leadership across the entire apprenticeship journey, from programme development and employer engagement to delivery, assessment and completion. You will help translate changing policy and regulatory expectations into effective systems, clear responsibilities and practical improvements. You will lead institutional development and continuous improvement of apprenticeship processes, working closely with the Head of Compliance and quality colleagues to strengthen data integrity, funding assurance, Ofsted readiness and evidence-led improvement. You will oversee programme performance, champion effective use of Aptem and related systems, and ensure that apprentice and employer feedback informs action. As a senior leader, you will build productive relationships with employers and sector partners, support new skills opportunities and work across academic and professional teams to address complex challenges. You will provide leadership and development for apprenticeship staff, promote inclusive practice and support financially sustainable provision. The role also includes leadership responsibilities within Aston Professional’s safeguarding arrangements. We are looking for someone with substantial experience of higher and/or degree apprenticeships and a strong record of leading apprenticeship quality, compliance, systems or delivery in a complex organisation. You will bring a sophisticated understanding of the apprenticeship policy and regulatory environment, experience of audit or inspection preparation, and the judgement to influence decisions across organisational boundaries. You will be an effective and collaborative leader, confident working with senior colleagues and employers, interpreting complex requirements and turning strategic priorities into measurable improvements. Strong analytical, communication and people-management skills, together with a commitment to inclusion, quality and continuous improvement, are essential. If you are motivated by the opportunity to strengthen apprenticeship quality, improve the apprentice and employer journey and help Aston Professional realise its ambitions, we would welcome your application. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role may meet the requirements for Skilled Worker visa sponsorship.If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting.See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills Head of Maintenance, Engineering & Infrastructure Clinical Senior Lecturer View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1890-26": {
      "title": "1890-26 Head of Maintenance, Engineering & Infrastructure",
      "description": "1890-26 Head of Maintenance, Engineering & Infrastructure - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register More ▼ Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Head of Maintenance, Engineering & Infrastructure Estates & Capital Developments Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £59,390 to £89,730\n            per annum Grade: Grade 10 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Friday 20 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 11 December 2026 Reference: 1890-26 Release Date: Friday 06 November 2026 Aston University is seeking an experienced leader to develop a customer-focused maintenance and infrastructure service that supports safe, reliable buildings and effective University operations. Reporting to the Director of Estates and Capital Development, you will lead multidisciplinary teams and specialist contractors across maintenance, engineering, utilities, grounds and the Estates Helpdesk. Your remit will cover all properties and grounds for which the directorate has maintenance responsibility. You will oversee planned and reactive maintenance, strengthen compliance assurance and emergency response, and develop costed maintenance and infrastructure investment plans. Working with Capital Projects colleagues, you will provide technical advice and ensure completed assets are ready for operational use. Improving service quality will be central to the role. You will set clear standards, develop your team and use customer feedback, asset information and digital systems to improve reliability, responsiveness and value. You will also evaluate opportunities for responsible automation and AI where these offer practical benefits. About you You will bring: Senior leadership experience across building fabric and engineering services within a complex, occupied estate. Experience managing statutory compliance, budgets, utilities, specialist contracts, emergency response and business continuity. A record of improving customer experience and service performance, including implementing digital systems or automated workflows. Inclusive leadership, sound technical judgement and the ability to provide clear risk advice and investment recommendations to senior decision-makers. A relevant degree or equivalent professional qualification, substantial relevant experience, appropriate professional membership or equivalent standing, and a recognised health and safety qualification or equivalent demonstrable competence supported by training. Experience in higher education or another complex operational environment is desirable, as is Chartered or Incorporated professional registration. You will maintain a visible presence across the estate and participate in the formal out-of-hours on-call rota, including attending campus when required under agreed arrangements. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 22 July 2025.  If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting.See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online Anonymous shortlisting will be carried out for this role as part of Aston University’s commitment to equality and diversity and ensuring a fair and consistent approach to recruitment. Personal details that are included on application forms, including the candidate’s name and address will not be disclosed to the shortlisting panel. CVs will not be considered as part of the shortlisting process. The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills Head of Maintenance, Engineering & Infrastructure Clinical Senior Lecturer View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
