    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1773-26": {
      "title": "Professor",
      "description": "1773-26 Professor - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Professor School of Engineering & Innovation Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £68,626 to £106,806\r\n            per annum Grade: Band 01 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 14 December 2026 Interview Date: Monday 18 January 2027 Reference: 1773-26 Release Date: Tuesday 10 November 2026 The Civil and Logistics Engineering Department is a growing and ambitious department within the School of Infrastructure & Built Environment, with expertise spanning Civil Engineering, Transport, Logistics and Engineering Management. We are seeking an enthusiastic and motivated Professor of Civil Engineering, to strengthen our research profile, expand our engagement with industry and regional partners, raise our external profile and further develop our programme portfolio. The successful applicant will lead research growth, and contribute to a positive and supportive student experience, as well as building greater external engagement in Civil Engineering and related areas. We particularly welcome applicants whose expertise complements existing departmental strengths and who can connect Civil Engineering with the challenges facing the West Midlands, including infrastructure renewal, brownfield regeneration, safe & resilient transport networks, sustainable construction, ground risk, climate adaptation and the transition to net zero. We are particularly interested in candidates who can provide strategic academic leadership to translate interdisciplinary research excellence into externally funded programmes, impactful partnerships and measurable benefits for the region’s infrastructure, economy and communities.  Whilst the fit of the candidates’ expertise to the department’s current strengths and future vision is important, we are particularly interested in candidates who will provide inclusive & effective research leadership across the department. We place a strong emphasis on team-working, collaboration, collegiality, student opportunity and making a tangible contribution to the School, University and wider community. The successful candidate will be expected to build constructive relationships with students, colleagues, professional bodies, employers, local authorities, consultancies and other regional stakeholders. A key aspect of the role will be to help establish Aston University as a regional hub for Civil Engineering knowledge, skills and innovation. This includes working with stakeholders to create authentic learning experiences and new pathways into civil and geotechnical engineering for students across the region. For informal enquiries about the role, please contact Dr Lucy Rackliff (L.Rackliff@Aston.ac.uk) What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 31 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Professor Technician Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1767-26": {
      "title": "Technician",
      "description": "1767-26 Technician - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Technician School Operations (COO) Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £31,861 to £37,369\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 07 Contract Type: Permanent Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 30 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 11 December 2026 Reference: 1767-26 Release Date: Tuesday 10 November 2026 Join Aston University as an Electrical/Electronics Technician and become part of a collaborative technical team supporting teaching, research and project-based learning. This hands-on role offers the opportunity to work closely with students, academics and researchers, turning ideas into practical solutions through electrical and electronic design, prototyping and testing. You will provide practical technical support for teaching laboratories, research and student projects. Key responsibilities include delivering laboratory demonstrations, supporting circuit design and troubleshooting, designing and testing electronic systems and prototypes, maintaining and repairing equipment, and helping manage laboratory components and consumables. You will also support safe working practices and contribute to maintaining well-organised, effective laboratory environments. You will have a relevant Electrical/Electronic Engineering qualification or equivalent practical experience, together with experience in a similar technical environment. You should have knowledge of electronics CAD packages such as KiCAD or Proteus, PCB design, Arduino/Raspberry Pi, programming such as C or Python, and hand soldering. Strong communication, problem-solving and organisational skills are important, along with the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Experience in electronic prototyping or power electronics would be advantageous. Due to the timeframe of the role, we are looking to appoint as soon as possible. We welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates and would particularly welcome those who are available to start at short notice. What we offer: Aston University is a vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Hybrid working is possible for this role, which means working both on campus and from home depending on the activity. Further information on hybrid working can be found here . Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days of bank holiday and University closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family-friendly policies. On-site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available. Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor those who are already on a Skilled Worker Visa issued before 04 April 2024 or 22 July 2025 and eligible for new entrant salary discount. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Professor Technician Assoc Dean - Apprenticeships & Skills View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1722-26": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow in Law",
      "description": "1722-26 Teaching Fellow in Law - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Teaching Fellow in Law School of Law & Social Sciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £38,784 to £46,970 Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (36 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 25 November 2026 Interview Date: Friday 11 December 2026 Reference: 1722-26 Release Date: Wednesday 04 November 2026 Join a distinctive and ambitious Law School Aston Law School is a friendly, inclusive and growing Law School located in the heart of Birmingham. We pride ourselves on delivering high-quality, practice-informed legal education that equips students with the knowledge, skills and confidence to succeed in an increasingly dynamic legal and professional environment. We are committed to providing an outstanding student experience through innovative teaching, strong student support and a focus on employability, social mobility and real-world impact. As part of our continued growth, we are seeking an enthusiastic and student-focused colleague who shares our passion for legal education and who will contribute to the ongoing development of our undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. This is an exciting opportunity to join a supportive and collegiate academic community where teaching excellence is valued and where colleagues are encouraged to develop their educational expertise and professional practice. About the role The successful candidate will play a key role in the delivery and enhancement of teaching across Aston Law School's undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. You will contribute to the design, delivery and assessment of modules, support student learning and development, and help create an engaging and inclusive learning environment for students from diverse backgrounds. You will contribute to curriculum enhancement, module development and quality assurance activities, while working collaboratively with colleagues across the School. The role also involves supporting student attainment, progression and employability, making effective use of educational technologies, and engaging in scholarly and professional activities that enhance teaching quality and student outcomes. In particular, we are looking for colleagues to contribute to the teaching activities of Aston Law School primarily in one or more of the areas below, whether independently or as part of a team: Land law Professional skills such as advocacy, legal writing, legal research, legal drafting, client interviewing About you You will hold a qualifying law degree or equivalent legal qualification and have experience of teaching and assessment in higher education. You will be committed to delivering an excellent and inclusive student experience, with the ability to engage and support students from diverse backgrounds. You will have experience of developing teaching materials, using digital technologies to enhance learning, and contributing to module or curriculum development. You will be an effective communicator who enjoys working collaboratively with colleagues and students and is committed to professional development and continuous improvement in legal education. Fellowship of Advance HE (or a willingness to obtain it) and postgraduate study in Law or a related discipline are desirable. Informal queries are welcome to Dr. Kristie Thomas, Head of Aston Law School: k.thomas5@aston.ac.uk Please visit our website Aston University Jobs for further information and to apply online. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers. Great family friendly policies. On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . Aston University may be able to sponsor the successful candidate if they are eligible for one of the salary discount options. Please see here for details about when you can be paid less for a Skilled Worker visa: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa/when-you-can-be-paid-less&nbsp ; Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Teaching Associate Postdoctoral Research Assistant Professor View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1902-26": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Assistant",
      "description": "1902-26 Postdoctoral Research Assistant - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Postdoctoral Research Assistant Institute of Health & Neurodevelopment Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £41,885 to £46,970\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (48 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 11 January 2027 Interview Date: Friday 29 January 2027 Reference: 1902-26 Release Date: Wednesday 11 November 2026 Worldwide, three people are diagnosed with encephalitis every minute—and autoimmune/immune-mediated causes are now just as common as infectious ones. While earlier immunotherapy often resolves acute symptoms like seizures, children remain disproportionately affected by devastating, long-term neuropsychiatric and sleep disorders. We are seeking an ambitious Postdoctoral Researcher to join a Wellcome-funded programme bridging this critical research gap. You will use preclinical experimental disease models and advanced electrophysiology to uncover how acute synaptic and neuro-immune disruptions drive persistent brain network changes—and identify new therapeutic targets to improve long-term outcomes for children. Working closely with an embedded clinical research team collecting longitudinal neuroimaging and cognitive data in children and young people, you will form part of a truly translational team. Key Responsibilities Drive Translational Discovery: Establish and characterise experimental models of paediatric autoimmune encephalitis to decode the cellular, synaptic, and network mechanisms behind chronic symptoms and test potential therapies. Investigate Circuit Function: Perform whole-cell patch clamp and local field potential recordings to uncover synaptic and circuit dysfunction. Capture Live Network Activity: Conduct stereotaxic surgeries to implant wireless EEG transmitters and osmotic pumps, analysing in vivo network connectivity and sleep/behavioural phenotypes. Explore Neuro-Immune Crosstalk: Investigate how microglia and disrupted neuro-immune signalling drive persistent structural and network changes, contributing to complementary molecular analyses. Manage Colony Operations: Oversee a genetically modified colony (breeding, genotyping, and accurate record-keeping) in strict compliance with Home Office regulations. Share Impact & Foster a Positive Research Culture: Publish in peer-reviewed journals, present at international conferences, and engage with stakeholders and the public, while supporting a safe, inclusive, and sustainable lab environment. About You You will hold a PhD in neuroscience, physiology, pharmacology, or a related discipline. Strong hands-on experience in in vitro and/or in vivo electrophysiology and stereotaxic surgical techniques is essential, alongside familiarity with UK Home Office regulatory compliance. You bring advanced analytical skills, a collaborative mindset, and a commitment to open, reproducible science. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role is likely to qualify for endorsement under the Endorsed Funder route of the Global Talent visa. This visa is for talented or promising individuals in academia or research in fields such as science, engineering, medicine, social sciences, or humanities. See the Home Office guidance: https://www.gov.uk/global-talent Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Teaching Associate Postdoctoral Research Assistant Professor View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1900-26": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate",
      "description": "1900-26 Teaching Associate - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Teaching Associate School of Law & Social Sciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £39,560 to £46,970 Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (18 months) Basis: Part Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Wednesday 25 November 2026 Interview Date: Monday 07 December 2026 Reference: 1900-26 Release Date: Wednesday 11 November 2026 Inspire critical thinking. Shape future perspectives. Make an impact through teaching and research-led education. Aston University is seeking an enthusiastic and dedicated Lecturer in Politics and International Relations to join the Department of Society and Politics, within the School of Law and Social Sciences. This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in the delivery and development of our Politics and International Relations curriculum, contributing to an engaging, inclusive and high-quality student learning experience. The successful candidate will take a lead role in delivering specialist modules, particularly South Asian Politics, Politics and Islam, and Research Methods in Political Science , while contributing to wider teaching and learning activities across the Department. You will bring subject expertise, innovative teaching approaches and a commitment to academic excellence, inspiring students to think critically, engage in debate and explore contemporary political and international issues. We are looking for someone who is passionate about student development, committed to delivering high-quality teaching and assessment, and keen to contribute to a supportive, collaborative and inclusive academic environment. Join Aston University and help shape the next generation of critical thinkers and informed global citizens. Apply now to be part of our academic community. Further details: Job Details Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Teaching Associate Postdoctoral Research Assistant Professor View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1777-26": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "1777-26 Research Associate - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Research Associate Aston Digital Futures Institute Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £39,560 to £46,970\r\n            per annum Grade: Grade 08 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (8 months) Basis: Full Time Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 14 December 2026 Interview Date: Monday 21 December 2026 Reference: 1777-26 Release Date: Thursday 12 November 2026 An excellent opportunity has arisen for an experienced and motivated games researcher to join our multidisciplinary team of researchers. The successful applicant will be affiliated with the Sir Peter Rigby Digital Futures Institute and work on computer games, digital twins, gamification and simulation systems. Flexible hybrid and remote working arrangements are supported. The researcher will take independent responsibility for a range of simulation and visualisation projects involving the development of computer games, digital twins in smart cities, gamification for rehabilitation and Virtual and Augmented Reality systems to simulate climate change. By programming in a game engine, they will contribute to the methodological and scientific delivery of the research, ensuring high standards of data quality and research governance, and play an active role in hands-on games projects, data analysis, academic publications and dissemination. The role will also involve contributing to research funding applications, supporting the supervision of postgraduate students and collaborating with researchers, clinical partners and industry partners across the UK and Europe. We welcome applications from candidates with a Master’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Games, Software Engineering, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline, alongside relevant research experience in games. A PhD in Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence or a related discipline would be advantageous. Previous research publication experience is essential, with a strong record of publications relevant to games research being particularly advantageous. The post is funded by SPR-DFI for 8 months, subject to continued funding and successful progression beyond the trial period. The anticipated start date for this role is early January 2027; however, a start date in early February 2027 may be considered. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here . This role may meet the requirements for Skilled Worker visa sponsorship. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role. Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skilled-worker-visa Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Senior Teaching Fellow (Deputy Programme Director- Physician Associates) Research Associate Teaching Associate View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    },
    "https://jobs.aston.ac.uk/Vacancy.aspx?ref=1893-26": {
      "title": "Senior Teaching Fellow (Deputy Programme Director- Physician Associates)",
      "description": "1893-26 Senior Teaching Fellow (Deputy Programme Director- Physician Associates) - Jobs at Aston Skip to main content Login Register Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use Contact Us Cookies Accessibility Search Jobs Jobs Aston Home Login Register Cookies This site requires the use of cookies as defined by our Terms and Conditions . \r\n        We have provided a detailed description of how cookies work and are used on the site . \r\n        To accept cookies, please click the \"Accept Cookies\" button. Accept Cookies Senior Teaching Fellow (Deputy Programme Director- Physician Associates) Medicine, Pharmacy & Biosciences Location: Aston University Main Campus Salary: £48,337 to £68,817\r\n            per annum (pro-rata) Grade: Grade 09 to Grade 10 Contract Type: Fixed Term\r\n              \r\n                (14 months) Basis: Part Time\r\n            (0.9) Closing Date: 23.59 hours GMT on Monday 30 November 2026 Interview Date: Wednesday 09 December 2026 Reference: 1893-26 Release Date: Thursday 12 November 2026 We are seeking an experienced and motivated academic or clinical educator to join the Physician Associate programme as Deputy Programme Director on a fixed-term basis to provide maternity cover for the Co-Programme Director. This is an exciting opportunity to take a significant leadership role within the programme, working closely with the Programme Director and wider programme team to ensure the effective delivery, coordination and development of the programme. Working under the strategic leadership and oversight of the Programme Director , the successful candidate will provide senior operational leadership across the programme during the period of maternity leave. They will play a key role in maintaining stability, continuity and effective decision-making across a busy postgraduate healthcare programme. What you will be doing The Deputy Programme Director will support the Programme Director in the effective academic and operational management of the programme, with responsibilities including: providing day-to-day operational leadership and oversight of programme delivery; supporting the coordination and delivery of the curriculum across the academic year; providing senior oversight of assessment processes, including the planning and delivery of written and clinical assessments; supporting student progression, academic performance and appropriate management of complex student matters; contributing to programme quality assurance, monitoring and enhancement activities; supporting the coordination of academic and clinical teaching staff and effective allocation of programme responsibilities; working collaboratively with colleagues involved in clinical placements and supporting effective integration between university-based and placement learning; contributing to admissions and recruitment activity; supporting the Programme Director with programme planning, operational decision-making and the management of emerging issues; contributing to relevant programme, School and University committees and activities; supporting appropriate engagement with external stakeholders and the wider Physician Associate education community; and deputising for the Programme Director where appropriate and within delegated areas of responsibility. About you You will be an experienced healthcare professional, academic or clinical educator with a strong understanding of postgraduate healthcare education. You will bring experience of working within complex educational environments and demonstrate the ability to coordinate multiple areas of activity while maintaining a strong focus on academic standards, student experience and effective programme delivery. We are particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate: substantial experience in healthcare or clinical education; experience of curriculum delivery and development; experience of assessment within higher education or professional healthcare education; an understanding of quality assurance and academic governance; experience of supporting students across their academic and professional development; the ability to provide effective leadership within a multidisciplinary academic and clinical team; strong organisational and problem-solving skills; excellent communication and interpersonal skills; the ability to manage competing priorities and make appropriate decisions in a complex programme environment; and the ability to work collaboratively with senior colleagues while exercising appropriate autonomy within delegated areas of responsibility. Experience of Physician Associate education and an understanding of the contemporary regulatory and professional context for Physician Associate training would be particularly valuable. Why this role matters The Deputy Programme Director will provide an important point of continuity for the programme during a period of maternity leave. The postholder will work in partnership with the Programme Director to ensure that the programme continues to operate effectively across teaching, assessment, student support, staffing, placements, admissions and quality assurance. This is therefore much more than a teaching-cover position. It provides an opportunity to gain or further develop programme-level academic leadership experience , contribute to the strategic and operational development of Physician Associate education and work collaboratively with academic, clinical and professional colleagues. Contract This appointment is offered on a fixed-term basis for 14 months to provide maternity cover . The duration of the appointment is intended to support effective continuity of programme leadership, including appropriate handover and transition around the substantive postholder's period of maternity leave. What we offer: Aston University is a dynamic and vibrant campus located within Birmingham city centre, which has excellent transport links via bus or train. Excellent training and development opportunities. A generous annual leave scheme with 30 days bookable leave and a further 13 days bank holiday and University Closure days. Everyday discounts to a number of activities and retailers Great family friendly policies On site gym and pool with discounted staff membership available Further information on our Benefits and Rewards can be found here This role may meet the requirements for Skilled Worker visa sponsorship. If you require sponsorship, Aston University will assess eligibility if you are shortlisted for the role.  Please note we are unable to confirm individual eligibility before shortlisting. See here for more information on Skilled Worker visa eligibility: https://www.gov.uk/skille Further details: Job Description Email details to a friend Apply Online The University celebrates the rights of freedom of speech and academic freedom and is committed to maintaining and protecting these rights within the law. An offer to work at Aston University will never be denied on the basis of an individual’s lawful expression of their beliefs, ideas or opinions. Aston University is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all sections of the community.  It promotes equality and diversity in all aspects of its work. We strive to have robust inclusivity strategies in place, to encourage colleagues to have the confidence and freedom to be themselves in the workplace. For more information, visit: https://www2.aston.ac.uk/about/inclusive-aston Guidance on AI-Assisted Applications While we cannot prevent applicants from using AI tools to support their application, we ask that all submissions reflect your own experience, achievements, and motivations. We want to understand what you personally bring to the role, so please ensure your application represents your own voice and capabilities. We recognise the value of flexible working.  Please contact the recruiting manager to discuss what flexible working options are available for particular roles. If you require the job details document or an application form in an alternative format please contact the recruitment team at recruitment@aston.ac.uk Share: View All Vacancies Login Please note: Javascript must be enabled to use this website. Email / Username: Password: I accept cookies Login Forgotten Details Register Find Jobs Jobs by Email Jobs by RSS Search Jobs: Search Advanced Job Search Latest Vacancies Senior Teaching Fellow (Deputy Programme Director- Physician Associates) Research Associate Teaching Associate View All Vacancies Jobs Current Vacancies Working at Aston Human Resources Website Terms of Use | Contact Us | Cookies | Accessibility © 2026 Aston University"
    }
  },
